#. macro: <if ($n1 < 300)>Less than 5 minutes<else><if ($n1 < 600)>Less than 10 minutes<else><if ($n1 < 1200)>Less than 20 minutes<else>Unknown. Servers are currently con… — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 1 < 300 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($n1 < 600)>Less than 10 minutes<else><if ($n1 < 1200)>Less than 20 minutes<else>Unknown. Servers are currently congested.</if></if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 1 < 600 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($n1 < 1200)>Less than 20 minutes<else>Unknown. Servers are currently congested.</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 1 < 1200 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
